This idea came to me at 3am in the morning, so forgive me if it's a
little sketchy:

The shopping cart is a tool that resembles a leash and a container
mashed together; it's a portable storage space that you can have
attached to your character.

The exact method of attaching it to oneself is undecided as of yet,
but ideas include:
 > attacking it while bare-handed
 > (c)losing it (closing your hands around the handle)
 > #untrapping it (not a good idea, as it could occupy the same square
as a trap)

The uses of the shopping cart are numerous:
 > paying for the contents of all items in a shopping cart at once
 > carrying objects around in it, without being burdened by them
 > #riding in it (fragile items may break)

Putting items in a shopping cart is done in the same way as regular
containers, that is, by #looting or (a)pplying them; however, shopping
carts cannot be locked as they have no lid.

Riding a shopping cart would behave in much the same way as riding a
pet, except for a penalty to accuracy (when was the last time you
tried to hit something while in a moving shopping cart?). Jumping on a
square with a cart on it would have the same affect as #riding it from
an adjacent square.

Any suggestions as to how this could work would be much appreciated.

